\check q Error
\submenu Phil_new
\script q_error.py
\description Find poetry lines (\q, \q1, \q2) with structural problems: final punctuation followed by text; two verse markers on one line; text before a verse marker; or (optionally) non-final punctuation with a single trailing word before the next poetry line. Footnotes (\f), cross-references (\x), and \qs content are ignored. Options let you toggle each sub-check on/off and adjust punctuation characters and thresholds.
\books
\noText
\toList
\utf8

\optionName FinalPunctuation
\optionLocalizedName Final punctuation characters
\optionDescription Characters that should end a poetry line. Flags any \q/\q1/\q2 line where one of these is followed by a word character. Default is period, exclamation mark, and question mark.
\optionDefault .!?

\optionName MinCharsBeforePunct
\optionLocalizedName Minimum characters before final punctuation
\optionDescription Ignore final punctuation that appears fewer than this many characters into the poetry line text. Use this to suppress false positives on very short lines. Set to 0 to check all lines regardless of length.
\optionDefault 0

\optionName NonFinalPunctuation
\optionLocalizedName Non-final punctuation characters
\optionDescription Used only when "Flag hanging word" is Yes. Characters considered mid-line (non-final) punctuation.
\optionDefault ,;:

\optionName CheckFinalPunct
\optionLocalizedName Flag final punctuation followed by text?
\optionDescription Choose No to disable checking for final punctuation followed by a word character on the same poetry line.
\optionDefault Yes

\optionName CheckDoubleVerse
\optionLocalizedName Flag multiple verse markers in one poetry line?
\optionDescription Choose No to disable checking for two \v markers within a single \q/\q1/\q2 line (same line or continuing to the next line).
\optionDefault Yes

\optionName CheckTextBeforeVerse
\optionLocalizedName Flag text before verse marker?
\optionDescription Choose No to disable checking for text content appearing before a \v marker in a poetry line. Normal form is \q1 \v N text; bad form is \q1 text \v N.
\optionDefault Yes

\optionName CheckHangingWord
\optionLocalizedName Flag line ending with punctuation + single word?
\optionDescription Choose Yes to flag any poetry line that ends with non-final punctuation followed by exactly one word (nothing else before end of line). May indicate the final word belongs on the following line.
\optionDefault No
